  "goodToKnow": "Die Gefangenschaft is captivity: in Gefangenschaft geraten (to be taken captive), Tiere in Gefangenschaft (in zoos). After 1945, millions of German soldiers were in Kriegsgefangenschaft. The last 10,000 returned from the Soviet Union in 1955–56 after Chancellor Adenauer's visit to Moscow, an emotional moment in West German history. Der/die Gefangene is a prisoner. It has no plural."
